    "title": "1 man killed in crash Wednesday on EB I-70 at Woods Chapel Road in Blue Springs - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By KSHB 41 News Staff ,\n8 hours ago A 28-year-old Independence man died in a traffic crash Wednesday afternoon on Interstate 70 just east of Woods Chapel Road in Blue Springs.\nThe eastbound lanes of the interstate at Woods Chapel Road were closed for about three hours; the area reopened around 6:30 p.m.\n1 dead in crash Wednesday on EB I-70 at Woods Chapel Road in Blue SpringsA crash report posted Wednesday night on the Missouri State Highway Patrol's website states the 28-year-old man died when his 2014 BMW X3 crashed into the back of a 2020 Volvo tractor-trailer.\nThe driver of the tractor-trailer, a 38-year-old man from Hollywood, California, was not injured.\nMSHP does not release the names of victims involved in traffic crashes.\n—\nIf you have any information about a crime, you may contact your local police department directly. But if you want or need to remain anonymous, you should contact the Greater Kansas City Crime Stoppers Tips Hotline by calling 816-474-TIPS (8477), submitting the tip online or through the free mobile app at P3Tips.com . Depending on your tip, Crime Stoppers could offer you a cash reward.\nAnnual homicide details and data for the Kansas City area are available through the KSHB 41 News Homicide Tracker , which was launched in 2015. Read the KSHB 41 News Mug Shot Policy .\n10",
